      "message": "De we need this in addition to `fMaxAllocation`?  If we redefine `fMaxAllocation` to be cumulative (instead of single allocation), it seems it would provide an equivalent signal.\n\nThe reason I prefer the former is this estimation would require us to duplicate the complex decision tree of how the decoder is set up (do we need a swizzler buffer?  how about a color transform buffer? etc), whereas we can perform `fMaxAllocation` accounting inline, as we decode, and fail the decode operation if we overflow.",
